WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:44.700
Speaker 1: The NAACP has issued issued&nbsp;
a travel advisory in response to Ron&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:51.480
Desantis's attempts to ban books about race&nbsp;
and LGBTQ identity, reject a new AP class on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:57.060
African-American studies, ban diversity, equity&nbsp;
and inclusion programs in Florida colleges.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:04.320
Quote Florida is openly hostile to&nbsp;
African-Americans, people of color, LGBTQ&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:08.700
plus individuals. Before traveling to Florida,&nbsp;
please understand that the state of Florida&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:14.220
devalues and marginalizes the contributions of&nbsp;
and the challenges faced by African-Americans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:19.680
and other communities of color. And it also&nbsp;
says if you decide to travel to Florida,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:25.080
be advised, Florida public schools won't teach&nbsp;
your children accurate African-American history.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.780
The state of Florida does not value diversity,&nbsp;
equity and inclusion. The state of Florida&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:33.900
doesn't welcome the contributions of&nbsp;
African-Americans as people of color,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:41.280
etc., etc., etc.. So a few different things to&nbsp;
this. On the one hand, sort of proving the point.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:48.960
I saw wildly racist responses to this online,&nbsp;
including people saying, Hey, Florida's only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:54.180
dangerous because of the black people. Maybe&nbsp;
this will keep black people out of the state.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.180 --> 00:02:00.900
The right wing subreddit conservative was openly&nbsp;
celebrating. Hey, you know what? We should welcome&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:07.140
this. This might make it so fewer black people&nbsp;
travel to Florida. Although the Post said less&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:12.300
black people rather than fewer. But I'm giving&nbsp;
it to you in a grammatically correct way. So a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:19.740
couple of different aspects to this. First of all,&nbsp;
the very reaction to this advisory by the NAACP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:28.620
proves much of what the NAACP is saying, period,&nbsp;
End of story. Secondly, the fact that in the U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:37.320
there are travel warnings to different states&nbsp;
based on this sort of thing, points to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:44.820
retrograde and backwards nature of what's going&nbsp;
on in the United States. But lastly, as a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:50.280
travel advisory, I don't know, like, for example,&nbsp;
the first thing on the list is be aware that if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:56.580
you travel to Florida, your kids aren't going&nbsp;
to be taught X, Y, Z. Most people traveling to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:02.820
Florida are going on vacation. They're not putting&nbsp;
their kids in school. So I hesitate to take this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:09.420
completely seriously as a literal travel advisory.&nbsp;
But I think the point here is to be more than a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:14.520
literal travel advisory. The idea here is bring&nbsp;
attention to what's going on in Florida. Point to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:18.900
how these policies in Florida disproportionately&nbsp;
impact marginalized communities of all kind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:24.300
Black folks, folks, LGBT folks, women. When it&nbsp;
comes to the abortion ban that has been passed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:30.840
and their families, of course. So I see this&nbsp;
advisory not, as you know, the advisory that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:35.280
U.S. State Department has about traveling to the&nbsp;
Sinaloa region of Mexico, where they say, listen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.740
significant cartel activity, if you get into&nbsp;
trouble there, you may be beyond help from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:47.160
U.S. embassy. This is not that. This is not that.&nbsp;
But it is a form of activism that raises awareness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:51.600
and it encourages dialog and the need for rights&nbsp;
and protections and points to many of the things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:56.580
that are going on, going on and going wrong in the&nbsp;
state of Florida. Now, there are people who saw&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:01.200
this advisory and said, this is very unfair.&nbsp;
This is very unfair to Florida as a whole,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:07.320
because you have so many parts of Florida where&nbsp;
even if it is the case that on paper teachers are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:13.620
not allowed to do X, Y, Z, it is actually in the&nbsp;
liberal parts of Florida. It is welcomed. Nobody&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:19.140
is blowing the whistle. You look at places like&nbsp;
Miami and Miami Beach and other liberal areas. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:25.020
LGBT community is welcome. There are absolutely no&nbsp;
risk danger whatsoever. Black folks are welcomed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:29.640
And I have to tell you, having spent time in those&nbsp;
areas, I believe that that's true. But still,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:37.140
it's really important to understand the underlying&nbsp;
message here. Even if state decrees from DeSantis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:42.000
are being ignored in the liberal parts of&nbsp;
Florida, which to a great degree they are.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.600 --> 00:04:50.280
It is still the case that as a state, Florida&nbsp;
is not fostering inclusivity, it's not promoting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:56.160
equality, it's not combating discrimination.&nbsp;
In fact, it seems to be building it. So I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.940 --> 00:05:03.360
let's not dismiss this outright because it's not&nbsp;
a literal travel advisory per the interpretation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:09.480
of some. Let's use it to remind ourselves&nbsp;
of the right wing hellscape that DeSantis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:16.080
is trying to turn Florida into. He hasn't yet&nbsp;
succeeded, certainly not in all parts of Florida,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.080 --> 00:05:22.080
but that's not a reason to ignore this. So a very&nbsp;
interesting declaration from the NAACP. We're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:28.140
going to take a quick break. We have a packed&nbsp;
program today. I do want to remind you that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:34.020
are just one week away from Monday, Memorial Day&nbsp;
on Monday, Memorial Day this year. That will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

